# VAISHMEDIALAB
# VAISHMEDIALAB

## Project Overview
VAISHMEDIALAB demonstrates GitHub repository governance, digital media asset management, cloud storage architecture, and digital asset security.

## Objectives
- Organize and manage digital media assets.
- Demonstrate Git version control and repository governance.
- Use Git Large File Storage (Git LFS) for large binary files.
- Document cloud storage architecture and cost optimization.
- Implement digital asset security practices.
- Document backup and recovery procedures.
- Explore digital watermarking techniques.

## Repository Structure

- `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATES/` - Issue templates for bug reports, feature requests, and tasks.
- `ASSETS/ANIMATIONS/` - Animation assets.
- `ASSETS/AUDIO/` - Audio files.
- `ASSETS/MODELS/` - 3D models and objects.
- `ASSETS/TEXTURES/` - Textures and images.
- `ASSETS/UI/` - User interface assets.
- `Documentation/` - Project documentation and security plans.
- `GIT-LFS/` - Git Large File Storage documentation.

## Technologies Used
- GitHub
- Git
- Git Large File Storage (Git LFS)
- Markdown
- Cloud storage concepts

## Documentation
The Documentation directory contains information about:
- Repository governance
- Media asset management
- Cloud storage architecture
- Cost optimization
- Digital watermarking
- Threat modeling
- Backup and recovery
- Project overview

## Security
The project emphasizes secure asset management, access control, version tracking, and backup planning.

## Conclusion
VAISHMEDIALAB provides a structured example of managing digital media assets through GitHub, version control, documentation, and cloud storage practices.
A project demonstrating GitHub repository governance, media asset management, cloud storage, and digital asset security.
